# ── credentials that arrive as FILES ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ This repo is public and AGPL. `.env` was covered; a downloaded credential
# was not, and a browser puts one wherever you last saved something.
#
# On 10 September 2026 a Firebase service-account key — a file that can send
# notifications as her — was downloaded straight into this directory. It was
# untracked, so nothing had happened yet; but every commit here is made with
# `git add -A`, which would have swept it into the next one and pushed it to a
# public remote. There is no undo for that: the key is burned the moment it
# lands, and the only fix is to revoke it at Google and issue another.
#
# So the patterns below are deliberately broad. A credential that is ignored
# by mistake costs nothing — you notice it is missing and move it. A
# credential committed by mistake costs a revocation and a redeploy.
*service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
*-adminsdk-*.json
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
*.pem
*.p8
*.p12
*.keystore
*.jks
